<h1>What is Physics?</h1>
<p><strong>Physics</strong> is the branch of science concerned with the nature and properties of matter and energy. It explains how things move, interact, and behave in the universe.</p>

<div class="highlight">
    <p>In simple terms: Physics helps us understand how the world and universe work.</p>
</div>

<h2>Examples of where we see physics in everyday life:</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Electricity (e.g., turning on lights, using a phone)</li>
    <li>Motion (e.g., cars driving, people walking)</li>
    <li>Sound (e.g., playing music, speaking)</li>
    <li>Light (e.g., vision, cameras, lasers)</li>
    <li>Technology (e.g., X-rays, satellites, computers)</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧠</span>Why is Physics Important?</h2>
<ul>
    <li>It explains how and why things happen in nature.</li>
    <li>It forms the foundation for engineering, technology, and other sciences.</li>
    <li>It helps develop problem-solving and analytical skills.</li>
    <li>It drives innovation and scientific discovery.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🔬</span>Branches of Physics</h2>
<p>Physics is divided into several branches based on the areas they study. Here are some examples:</p>

<table>
    <tr>
        <th>Branch</th>
        <th>Focus</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Mechanics</strong></td>
        <td>Motion, force, and energy of objects</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Thermodynamics</strong></td>
        <td>Heat, temperature, and energy transfer</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Electromagnetism</strong></td>
        <td>Electric and magnetic fields</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Optics</strong></td>
        <td>Behavior of light and vision</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Quantum Physics</strong></td>
        <td>Physics at the atomic and subatomic level</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Relativity</strong></td>
        <td>Space, time, and gravity in extreme conditions</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="emoji">🛠️</span>Getting Started with Physics</h2>
<p>To study physics effectively, you’ll need a few basic tools and resources.</p>

